    "reason": "A verdict was wanted sooner. Lowering minimum_complete_events would have delivered that and destroyed the verdict: at n=10 with profit_factor >= 1.2 a single good event carries the whole statistic, so 'accepted' would stop meaning anything. The acceptance threshold therefore does not move. An interim tier at 10 reports the same metrics early under INSUFFICIENT_DATA_NOT_REJECTED and is structurally unable to authorise: interim_authorizes is False and the validator requires interim_descriptive_events to sit strictly below minimum_complete_events, so the two tiers cannot be collapsed into one by later raising the interim number."
